# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# The real production env file docker-compose.prod.yml's `env_file:` expects
# (contains INTERNAL_API_SECRET, CHAT_SESSION_TOKEN_SECRET, DATABASE_URL,
# etc.) — was not previously ignored, meaning a real .env.production created
# at the repo root would have been eligible for accidental commit. Only
# .env.production.example (the template, no real secrets) should ever be
# tracked.
.env.production

